# Augur generation EVAL CANDIDATE — not a default. gemma4-e4b-12k stays the
# baseline (AUGUR_KNOWLEDGE_MODEL); this tag only gives an A/B eval profile a
# second generator to point at. Nothing creates or pulls it at boot.
#
# Qwen3.5-4B, Apache-2.0, 262K native context, from the official Ollama library
# (~3.4GB), so no hand-fetched GGUF is involved — swapping the candidate is this
# one FROM line. Build it by hand inside news-creator-backend:
#   ollama create qwen3.5-4b-12k -f Modelfile.qwen3.5-4b-12k
#
# The tag must keep the `qwen3` substring: rag-orchestrator's buildOptions picks
# sampling parameters by model-name substring, and an unmatched name falls to
# the temperature=0.2 default branch, which would skew the comparison.
FROM qwen3.5:4b

# Library tags carry their own template and stop tokens, so only the context
# window is pinned — matched to gemma4-e4b-12k so an A/B run compares
# generators, not context budgets.
PARAMETER num_ctx 12288
